# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# Plan 00185 Task 1.1 (#60, wrong emoji glyphs): TRIAGE ONLY, READ-ONLY. The plan has only
# triage.bash; it changes nothing on the host, needs no sudo and never prompts. It records the
# terminal it runs in and every running terminal emulator (version, start time), the VTE
# version, the emoji font packages and their install times, fc-match and fc-list for the
# issue's code points, the fontconfig cache ages, which emoji font file each running terminal
# has mapped, and the terminals' font and GPU settings. Start meta-deploy from the terminal that
# draws the wrong emoji, and leave that window open while it runs.
00185-terminal-emoji-glyphs
# play-basic-configs.yml (no plan owns it): the GRUB auto-hide probe fix is proven (the probe ran,
# the unset was skipped, changed=0), but the last two runs stopped at the fwupd task on an LVFS
# 503 (metadata refresh timed out through all retries), so the tasks after it (the ABRT policy
# onward) have not run. Run the whole play again; its
# other tasks (firmware updates among them) run too, as on any run. The same run rebuilds
# and installs git-fetch-age with Plan 00183's fix (an empty FETCH_HEAD, left by a fetch that
# failed, is marked [fetch failed or running] instead of being read as a fresh fetch).
playbooks/imports/play-basic-configs.yml
# Plan 00183 (#52, stale tracking ref in the prompt): triage.bash, then acceptance.bash, RE-RUN.
# The plays are deployed and five of six acceptance legs passed; the "deployed prompt shows the
# mark" leg failed on a checker bug (a prefix assignment to a readonly variable), now fixed.
# Both scripts are READ-ONLY, need no sudo and never prompt. The triage records the installed
# bash-git-prompt and its fetch settings, every FETCH_HEAD of this checkout with its size and
# age, the SSH agent's keys, and whether the remote answers with the agent and with none (git
# ls-remote with no terminal, so no passphrase can be asked; nothing is fetched). The
# acceptance checks the git-fetch-age and git-prompt-fetch the plays installed, in scratch
# repositories it makes and removes, with fetches through a failing ssh or a recording stand-in
# that reach no remote, and the interactive shell's async_run.
00183-prompt-shows-stale-tracking-ref
# Plan 00212 (pause media while recording): the whole speech-to-text play. It builds and installs
# the new wsi-pause-media command, deploys the panel extension with its new mediaHold.js and the
# "Pause media while recording" menu switch (on by default; new GSettings key), and installs
# python3-gobject and dbus-daemon (systemd's busctl is already there). The extension changes need
# a log out and back in. Before the 00212 acceptance.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-speech-to-text.yml
# Plan 00212 Task 3.1: acceptance.bash (no triage.bash or deploy.bash) runs the installed
# wsi-pause-media against a fake media player on a private session bus, so no real player is
# touched: paused and played again at TERM, left alone when stopped by hand, nothing done when
# nothing plays, and played again when its parent ends. No sudo, no prompts.
00212-stt-pauses-media-while-recording
# Plan 00211 Task 0.1 (reports and questions rooms): the SPIKE, a throwaway test. It starts the
# installed Tuwunel as you, on a free loopback port, with scratch accounts and rooms under its own
# run directory, and removes them when it ends. No unit, team, play or real homeserver is touched.
# It records whether a restricted join, the power-level refusals and a pending invite behave as the
# design needs, and whether the side rooms' power levels and join rules read back exactly; a fact
# that does not hold fails the run, and its report says which. Deploy 1 below runs either way (it
# makes no room); deploy 2 will refuse to run until a spike report says every fact holds.
00211-agent-bus-reports-and-questions-rooms/spike.bash
# Plan 00211 deploy 1 (Task 1.13), after the spike above: deploy.bash --stage 1, the member side
# only, so no room is created yet. It runs the whole play-agent-bus.yml (the host's pingbus
# becomes 0.2.0, which knows the reports and questions rooms, and every running LXC member's kit
# is copied again) and the whole play-claude-yolo.yml (the staged pingbus and skill, and the ccy
# image rebuilt once as container 2.78.7). Needs sudo once. Then acceptance.bash --stage 1
# checks the host's, the ccy build context's and each declared LXC container's pingbus version,
# and refuses a declared container that is down, naming it. The agent-bus play also fails, naming
# the entry, if a present LXC member is declared role coordinator with human_text false (a
# coordinator must read human text). Afterwards restart the teams'
# agent sessions so they run the new pingbus.
00211-agent-bus-reports-and-questions-rooms/deploy-stage-1.bash
